WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:18,160
How do I treat an infected, small wound from a bird? Well, you know, that's a tough question

00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:24,480
answer because it depends on how deep the bird is, what level of bird it is. If you're trying

00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:31,760
to, if you have an infected wound, there's topical, from a medical standpoint, there's obviously

00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:37,120
topical antibiotics, tributyptivatic appointments and things. From a natural perspective,

00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:44,240
a person could use honey. That could help heal a wound and kill infection. A person could use

00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:54,640
topical hydrogen peroxide. There's different topical treatments that are, if, if the wound is

00:00:54,640 --> 00:01:01,360
a closed wound, it's not open anymore. You could use cumpri, if it's a closed, if it's a closed

00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:09,360
wound, you could use calendula. There's other different appointments that a person could use on

00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:15,200
a wound. If it's a bird that needs to be treated, if it's a third degree bird or something like that,

00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:20,080
you're going to end up going into the ER that you don't want to be putting that anything on it

00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:26,000
until you get in there because they're going to scrape that off. But if you're, if that's not the

00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,200
case, and it's a small bird, and it's just a rule that seems to be festering and open,

00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:34,960
then you want to make sure that it doesn't get infected. So that's where

00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:42,720
a topical antibiotic, a hydrogen peroxide rate, but honey can be helpful in those cases.

